          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What do you "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "infer",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " from Case 2?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.106,
            0.747,
            0.209
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You may have learnt about iodised salt through newspapers, advertisements or by reading about it on a salt packet. What does it mean? Iodised salt is simply common salt mixed with required quantities of salts of iodine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.251,
            0.286,
            0.364
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.121,
                0.251,
                0.286,
                0.364
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_8_image_3.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.298,
            0.243,
            0.778,
            0.368
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Salt farming is a traditional practice of a tribal community named Agariyas. They practice salt farming in the Little Rann of Kutch and other parts of Gujarat. For eight months, they live in the extreme heat of the desert and work very hard to get salt from seawater."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.795,
            0.352,
            0.897,
            0.392
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "More to know!",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.413,
            0.744,
            0.458
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How would you find out more about other food components that protect our body from various diseases?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.469,
            0.51,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 3.4: Let us conduct a survey"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.503,
            0.744,
            0.617
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Study the chart given in Fig. 3.5 to explore the functions and sources of various food components. Find out more sources of vitamins and minerals. Also, understand the symptoms of the diseases caused by the lack of these food components."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.624,
            0.744,
            0.715
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Visit your neighbourhood, interact with people and find out if any individual shows the symptoms listed on the chart (an investigatory project of this kind can be taken by the students under the guidance of a teacher)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.721,
            0.743,
            0.767
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Correlate these symptoms with their diet and identify the deficiency disease(s) or disorder(s)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.773,
            0.743,
            0.818
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Suggest the possible cause(s) for the symptoms observed and changes required in the diet for improvement."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.825,
            0.675,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Suggest them to visit a doctor for further advice."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.873,
            0.753,
            0.913,
            0.868
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "to a Healthy Body Mindful Eating: A Path"
            }
          ]
